cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Asterion: deterministic C++20 market replay, L3 order books, price-time matching, pre-trade risk and inference evaluation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Naik
    given-names: Anannye
repository-code: "https://github.com/anannyenaik/asterion"
abstract: >-
  A C++20 systems lab for deterministic market replay, L3 order-book
  reconstruction, price-time-priority matching, pre-trade risk controls and
  inference evaluation. The event log, resulting book state, execution reports
  and diagnostics carry deterministic checksums, so optimisation paths such as
  the opt-in pooled order book and the bounded single-producer single-consumer
  replay pipeline are compared only after the relevant parity or benchmark guard
  checks agree. Scope is limited to recorded and simulated workloads.
keywords:
  - order book
  - matching engine
  - market data
  - deterministic replay
  - risk management
  - performance engineering
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
